The Mercedes-Benz CLS 350d V6 refers to the C218 generation (2011-2018) equipped with the 3.0L V6 diesel engine. There are slightly different power outputs and transmission types depending on the specific year and whether it's RWD or 4MATIC, and pre- or post-facelift. The most common is the 265 HP version with the 7G-Tronic Plus, or the 258 HP version with the 9G-Tronic after the 2014 facelift. I will use the specs for the 265 HP version (pre-facelift) as it's a prominent V6 diesel variant.

**Key Data Extracted (primarily from for 265 HP C218 350 CDI V6):**
*   **Engine:** 3.0L V6 Turbo Diesel (OM642)
*   **HP:** 265 HP
*   **Torque:** 620 Nm (457 lb-ft)
*   **Cylinder Count:** 6
*   **Engine Displacement:** 3.0L (2987 cm³)
*   **0-60 mph:** ~5.8-6.1 seconds
*   **Top Speed:** 155 mph (250 km/h)
*   **Drive Type:** RWD or 4MATIC AWD - Scoring for RWD as it's common, but AWD was available.
*   **Transmission Type:** 7-speed Automatic (7G-Tronic Plus) (9G-Tronic on later facelift 350d) - Scoring for 7G-Tronic Plus.
*   **Size (Length):** ~4940 mm (194.5 inches)
*   **Wheelbase:** ~2874 mm (113.1 inches)
*   **Body Style:** 4-door Coupe/Sedan
*   **Seats:** 4 (commonly cited for C218)
*   **Cargo Space:** ~520 Litres (~18.4 cu ft) (475L on facelift) - Using 520L.
*   **Rear Space:** Limited due to coupe roofline.
*   **Ground Clearance_in:** ~118 mm (~4.6 inches) (Range 3.7-5.1 inches found). Using 4.6 inches.
*   **Turn Radius_ft:** ~11.27 m (~37.0 ft) (Range 36.7-40.4 ft found). Using 37 ft.
*   **MPG:** Combined NEDC ~38.5-47 UK mpg (~32-39 US mpg). Real-world ~83% of official. Using a blend, leaning towards real-world (~30-35 US mpg).
*   **CO2_g_km:** 148-160 g/km.
*   **Electrification:** Diesel.
*   **Electric Range/Charge Speed:** N/A.
*   **Price (Used):** Varies greatly. Examples found range from ~€11k (~$12k) to ~€30k (~$33k). Averaging around $15,000-$25,000 for a typical used example.
*   **Insurance Group (UK):** 39-47. Using 43 as a mid-point.
*   **Maintenance/Repair Risk:** Mercedes maintenance is generally higher than average. The OM642 V6 diesel had some known issues (oil cooler leaks, intake manifold, turbo actuator). 7G-Tronic had early issues but improved. Overall, moderate risk for an older luxury diesel.
*   **ADAS:** Available features for the era included Lane Keep Assist and Blind Spot Assist. Less comprehensive than modern systems.
*   **Interior/Tech:** High quality interior materials for its time. Screen size and infotainment UX are dated compared to modern cars. Smartphone connectivity limited.
*   **Prestige:** Mercedes-Benz is high brand prestige. CLS is a step below S-Class but above E-Class (model prestige). 350 CDI V6 is a mid-range engine/trim for the CLS (trim prestige).

